{
 "esm": "1.0.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "RRTMGasOptics",
  "description": "The gaseous optical depths and Planck fractions of WRF's RRTM longwave scheme (SUBROUTINE GASABS and the sixteen band routines TAUGB1-TAUGB16 of phys/module_ra_rrtm.F, WRF 4.8) for the RRTM column of rrtm_column.esm, from the interpolation coefficients of rrtm_setcoef.esm. Every band interpolates its g-point-reduced k-tables (rrtm_kdist_bandNN.esm, transcribed from RRTM_DATA and the module's DATA statements) bilinearly in ln p and temperature with SETCOEF's weights, adds the water-vapour self continuum (linear in temperature between two SELFREF rows) and, where the band has one, the foreign continuum and minor absorbers (N2O as an excess over a reference atmosphere, CO2 through CO2MULT, the CFC/CCl4 cross sections, zero in WRF). Two-species bands add a third interpolation dimension, the species parameter ca/(ca + STRRAT cb), with band-specific re-binning of its intervals (bands 3, 4, 9). Layers 1..LAYTROP use the lower-atmosphere tables ABSA, the rest ABSB (band 8 switches at LAYSWTCH; bands 6, 12, 13, 15, 16 have no upper-atmosphere absorption). GASABS then quantises the diffusivity-weighted optical depth into the table index ITR = INT(5000 od/(BPADE + od) + 0.5) that rtrn_sweep.esm consumes. The scheme is diagnostic. Fortran INT() is written as floor() (every argument is non-negative). Because esm evaluates both branches of an ifelse, the table rows of the inactive lower/upper branch are clamped into range (jp_lo, jp_up); the clamped values never reach a result. The per-band outputs taug_bNN/pfrac_bNN are the tested quantities (the g-points of one band with the band's own tolerance); taug/pfrac/itr are their assembly over the 140 g-points. Reference: real32 WRF dumps (no standalone driver), tolerance contract rel 1e-5. Reference: Mlawer et al. (1997) JGR 102, 16663; WRF 4.8 phys/module_ra_rrtm.F lines 4483-6275 and 6721-6873."
 },
 "metaparameters": {
  "NLEV": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 59,
   "description": "Number of model layers (WRF kte); 59 for the em_scm_xy reference column."
  },
  "NBUF": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 44,
   "description": "Buffer layers MM5ATM adds above the model top (see rrtm_column.esm); 44 for the reference column. NLAYERS = NLEV + NBUF."
  },
  "NGPT": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 140,
   "description": "Number of g-points after the 256-to-140 reduction."
  }
 },
